# Welding Calculator — product rules

Live: https://welding-calc.vercel.app  
Stack: Next.js 16 App Router + React + TS + Tailwind + manual PWA (`public/sw.js`).

## Product

- Languages: **PL / EN only** (no Russian).
- Currencies: PLN / USD (+ EUR display via rate).
- Audience: welder doing **pipes** (water / hydraulic / air) + profiles. No sheet-metal / hardware catalogs.
- No markup/profit layer — profit is already in hour/cm rates.
- Auth / payments / accounts: **not yet** — do not add unless explicitly asked.
- Public client link: `/client#p=…` embeds hour rate + contacts (no backend).
- Estimates for shop quoting — not WPS / certification docs.

## Modes

- **full (shop):** materials + welding + tooling + labor.
- **onsite:** client materials — **hours only** (no dims/welding/tooling in UI or bill; delivery/VAT still OK).
- Prep work is a % on billed hours (default +35%, editable).
- Invoice: VAT toggle (editable %). Delivery optional.

## Data

- Client-only persistence in `localStorage`:
  - `welding-calc-v2` settings
  - `welding-calc-jobs-v1` jobs
  - `welding-calc-pricebooks-v1` price books
- Jobs/settings are **plaintext** at rest. Photos: allow only safe `data:image/...` URLs.
- After calc/storage/job changes: run `npx tsx scripts/smoke-check.ts` (and security-check when touching photos/storage).

## Deploy

- Production via `npx vercel --prod --yes` → https://welding-calc.vercel.app
- Friend uses the permanent Vercel URL (no Cloudflare tunnels).
